//@version=6
// initial_capital / default_qty_value below are STRATEGY-TESTER ONLY and are deliberately NOT
// the account. The tester trades ONE unit of the INDEX; the broker buys the "Option contracts"
// quantity of an OPTION. See "WARNING 0" — setting them to the real account silently deletes
// trades from the backtest.
strategy("SPX ORB 3-Bot v1 STRATEGY — Bot1 orders + spread alerts", shorttitle="SPX-ORB 3BOT S", overlay=true,
     initial_capital=100000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, max_labels_count=500)

// STATUS 2026-08-17 (v1.3.1): STRATEGY companion to pine/SPX_ORB_3BOT_v1.pine (same signals) —
// v1.3.1 (2026-08-17): TESTER SIZING FIX, no signal logic touched. initial_capital 20,000 ->
//   100,000 and default_qty_value 3 -> 1, so the Strategy Tester can always afford the position
//   and stops dropping trades. Found by auditing a real export — see WARNING 0. The BROKER
//   quantity ("Option contracts") is UNCHANGED at 3.
// v1.3.0 (2026-08-17): THIS IS NOW A ONE-BOT SYSTEM AT 3 CONTRACTS. Set on user instruction.
//   1. "Option contracts" 10 -> 3. See WARNING 1.
//   2. BOT2 and BOT3 spread alerts DEFAULT OFF (enB2/enB3 = false). They were never automatable
//      (single-leg webhooks only) and the decision is to run ONE bot. The code is left intact —
//      tick the two boxes to get the labels/alerts back. BOT3-LONG (the separate strategy file)
//      is likewise RETIRED, not deleted: do not put it on a chart.
//   3. NEW "Bot1 - Risk" group: a RELATIVE premium skip (default 0.70% of spot) replacing the
//      drifting fixed-$2,000 rule. Pine CANNOT read option prices, so this CANNOT block the
//      order — it computes and PRINTS the dollar threshold on the entry label and exposes it to
//      alerts. Enforcement is manual, or via TradersPost "Amount per position". See WARNING 3.
//   4. margin_long/margin_short REMOVED (were 33.333). See WARNING 2 — that number was
//      Strategy-Tester fiction and made the tester report leverage the broker will never grant.
// v1.2.2 (2026-08-17): account re-base to $20,000 / 10ct / 3x. Superseded by v1.3.0 above.
// v1.2.1 (2026-08-08): BOT1 entries blocked on the session's FINAL bar (15:55) — see the
//   `rthIx < 77` note at the signal block. No other change.
//
// *** WARNING 0 — NEVER SET initial_capital/default_qty_value TO YOUR REAL ACCOUNT. ***
// Measured on a real export (SPCFD:SPX, 2026-08-17, v1.3.0 defaults of $20,000 / 3 units):
//   The tester bought 3 units of the INDEX = ~$20,400 of notional against $20,000 of equity.
//   Median headroom $457, MINIMUM $14. 52 of 95 entries had under $500 to spare. THREE trades
//   were partially margin-called mid-position (filled at qty 1 and 2 instead of 3), and once SPX
//   crossed ~6,816 the tester could not open a 3-lot at all — it silently stopped trading on
//   2026-04-13 and showed nothing for the following four months.
//   Cross-checked against the OPRA backtest for the SAME window (2025-08-18..2026-04-13):
//   158 BOT1 signals existed. The export showed 95. **40% of the trades were missing**, with no
//   error anywhere — the equity curve just looked calm and short.
// The fix is NOT fake margin (see WARNING 2), it is to stop conflating the two numbers: the
// tester is a 1-unit INDEX TIMING PROXY on notional capital, and the only field that reaches the
// broker is "Option contracts". Keep tester capital far above 1x the index level.
//
// *** WARNING 1 — WHAT 3 CONTRACTS ON $20,000 ACTUALLY RISKS. ***
// Every backtest figure in this file is PER CONTRACT. Multiplied by 3 against a $20,000 account,
// WITHOUT the premium skip below:
//     BOT1 worst day   -$6,980/ct  ->  -$20,940   = 105% of the account   (single session)
//     BOT1 max DD     -$12,165/ct  ->  -$36,495   = 182% of the account
// WITH the 0.70%-of-spot skip active (the reason it is the default):
//     BOT1 worst day   -$2,230/ct  ->   -$6,690   = 33% of the account
//     BOT1 max DD      -$6,655/ct  ->  -$19,965   = 100% of the account
// So 3 contracts is survivable on a single bad DAY only if the skip is honoured, and the max
// drawdown is at the edge of the account either way. A shuffled-path ruin sim on 2026 puts
// P(ruin) at 1.1% with a minimum equity of $12,320 at 3ct+skip (it was 20.9% at 10ct). Premium
// at 3ct commits $2,400-$9,180 per entry (median $3,660); on 2026 pricing the account can always
// fund an entry, which was NOT true at 10ct (45% of 2026 sessions could not).
//
// *** WARNING 2 — LEVERAGE DOES NOT EXIST FOR THIS STRATEGY AT A BROKER. ***
// v1.2.2 briefly carried margin_long/margin_short=33.333 ("3x"). That only ever changed
// TradingView's Strategy Tester, so it has been REMOVED. Under Reg T a LONG option position is
// 100% CASH — not marginable at any leverage, 0DTE least of all. The broker rejects anything the
// cash balance cannot pay for outright. Buying power for this system is $20,000, not $60,000.
//
// *** WARNING 3 — THE PREMIUM SKIP IS THE LARGEST SINGLE SOURCE OF EDGE, AND PINE CANNOT ENFORCE IT. ***
// The rich-premium tercile is NET NEGATIVE (-$61,310, PF 0.77) and hosts every worst day. The old
// FIXED $2,000 rule drifts — it is a dollar threshold on a premium that scales with the index, so
// it tightened from 0.49% of spot in 2022 to 0.28% in 2026, and by now it is actively harmful:
//   no skip       : 2022 +58,425  2023 +63,415  2024 +14,775  2025 +40,715  2026 +28,235
//   skip > $2,500 : 2022 +99,190  2023 +96,510  2024 +18,930  2025 +11,575  2026  +5,865
// The RELATIVE cap now shipped as the default (0.70% of spot) fixes the drift: +$321,815 over
// 2022-2026 vs +$205,585 no-skip, PF 2.39, worst day -$2,230 vs -$6,980, max DD -$6,655 vs
// -$12,165, and it wins 4 of the 5 years. Walk-forward (each year's cap fit only on prior years)
// = +$183,490 vs +$147,080 over the 4 live years, so it is not a single hindsight-fit number.
// BUT: a Pine chart cannot see option prices. The strategy prints the dollar threshold and sends
// it with the alert; YOU (or TradersPost sizing) must apply it. If the ATM ask exceeds the
// printed number, SKIP THE TRADE.
//
// *** BOT2 / BOT3 / BOT3-LONG ARE RETIRED AS OF v1.3.0 (one-bot decision). ***
// BOT2/BOT3 credit spreads were never webhook-automatable (TradersPost is single-leg only) and
// now default OFF here. pine/SPX_ORB_BOT3L_60M_v1_strategy.pine (the 60m single-leg long) is
// retired too — leave it OFF the charts. If it is ever revived it MUST run as its own strategy on
// its own chart: TradingView nets positions within a strategy, and BOT1/BOT3 break in OPPOSITE
// directions on 25% of days, so a merged BOT3 entry would silently flatten an open BOT1.
//
// SEPARATE from the UDB-ORB TSLA suite. Chart: SPX, 5-minute, RTH.
// v1.1 CHANGES (no signal logic touched): header synced to the 2026-07-24 re-verification;
//   NEW "Option quantity mode" input (default = unchanged) wiring the fixed-DOLLAR sizing that
//   was validated on 2026-07-24 but never reached this file; exit JSON no longer hardcodes a
//   quantity (action=exit closes the whole position — required for sizing mode, and safer in
//   both modes since the strategy cannot know a broker-sized contract count).
// WHAT THIS AUTOMATES (via TradersPost webhook, Order asset = Options):
//   BOT1 15m OR break -> BUY ATM 0DTE (CALL up / PUT dn), and CLOSE at the 30-min TIME STOP
//   (or EOD failsafe). The +50%/-50% PREMIUM brackets are NOT chart-executable (the chart
//   cannot see option prices) — place them as a broker-side OCO after the fill, or manage
//   manually. The time stop + EOD exits ARE automated here.
//   BOT2/BOT3 credit spreads = ALERTS ONLY (multi-leg orders are not webhook-able here);
//   use the alertcondition()s and place the spread at the broker.
// Strategy Tester shows INDEX-POINT P&L of the Bot1 timing only (a proxy) — real option P&L
// (premium, theta, IV) is NOT backtestable in TV. HOW BIG THE GAP IS, measured on the
// 2025-08-18..2026-04-13 export: the tester showed +$453 on 95 trades (+2.27%, WR 52.6%,
// PF 1.38, +1.59 index points per unit per trade). OPRA over the same window, on the 158 trades
// that actually existed: +$30,755 @1ct / +$92,265 @3ct, WR 46.2%. Note the tester's win rate is
// HIGHER and its P&L ~200x smaller — the index is directionally right more often than the option
// is profitable (theta eats the small wins), and the option converts a 1.6-point index move into
// a leveraged premium move. NEVER read the tester's % return as the strategy's return.
//
// *** HOW TO VALIDATE A STRATEGY-TESTER RE-RUN (do this after every paste). ***
//   python scripts/spx_expected_trades.py
// It replays THIS state machine bar-for-bar on the cached SPX 5m bars and writes
// exports/spx/EXPECTED_bot1_trades_v131.csv (1,127 trades 2022-01-03..2026-07-16; it agrees
// with the OPRA backtest on direction for 100.00% of the 1,107 shared sessions). Reconcile the
// tester's trade LIST against it -- count, dates, directions. Expected per year: 2022 250 /
// 2023 246 / 2024 250 / 2025 250 / 2026 131 (part year). Structural invariants that must hold:
// entries 09:45-15:50 and NEVER 15:55, 1,123 of 1,127 exits are the 30m time stop at 6 bars,
// exactly one trade per session, 586 long / 541 short.
//   *** EXPECT A FLAT-TO-UGLY TESTER EQUITY CURVE -- THAT IS A PASS. *** Total index-point P&L
//   over 2022-2026 is +163.5 points (~+$163 at 1 unit) and NEGATIVE in 3 of the 5 years, while
//   the identical trades on real 0DTE options are +$205,025 @1ct, +$321,815 with the skip.
//   Judge the re-run on trade count and dates ONLY. Never on the curve.
//   NOTE the chart symbol matters: SPCFD:SPX (a CFD feed) breaks a few minutes off the index on
//   some days, so match dates and directions, not timestamps.
// The REAL numbers are the OPRA backtest,
// BARCLOSE-CORRECTED 2026-07-24 (the originals had a 5-min entry lookahead — bar-START quotes):
// FULL 2022-2026 @1ct: BOT1 ts30 +$205,025 (was +$457,265; WR 48%, PF 1.50, worst -$6,980),
// COMBO +$687,671 (was +$1,088,751). Every bot positive every year; see docs/SPX_ANALYSIS.md.
// SIZING (re-verified 2026-07-24, skip re-fit 2026-08-17): the RICH premium tercile is NET
// NEGATIVE (-$61,310, PF 0.77) and hosts the -$6,980 worst day. Skipping it is where the edge is.
// The fixed-$ form of that skip has DRIFTED and is now harmful (header WARNING 3); the shipped
// rule is the RELATIVE one — skip when ATM premium > 0.70% of spot — which returns +$321,815 vs
// +$205,585 no-skip over 2022-2026, wins 4 of 5 years, and holds up walk-forward.
// Forward ledger: forward_test_spx.py (daily, T+1; barclose-corrected + rebuilt same day).

// ==================== INPUTS ====================
bufPct     = input.float(0.05, "Break buffer (% of OR level)", minval=0.0, step=0.01, group="Signal") * 0.01
tsMin      = input.int(30, "Bot1 time stop (minutes)", minval=5, step=5, group="Bot1")
optQtyMode = input.string("Fixed contracts", "Option quantity mode", options=["Fixed contracts", "TradersPost sizing (omit quantity)"], group="Bot1 · TradersPost", tooltip="Fixed contracts (default) = the webhook sends the 'Option contracts' quantity below, i.e. v1.0 behaviour, unchanged. 'TradersPost sizing' = the entry JSON OMITS the quantity field so TradersPost's strategy-level position sizing decides the contract count — set 'Amount per position' to ~$2,000 there (= the $1k/day risk cap, since risk/ct is HALF the premium). WHY: the 2026-07-24 re-verification found the RICH premium tercile is net NEGATIVE (-$61,310, PF 0.77) and hosts the -$6,980 worst day; a $1k risk cap auto-skips those days for +$452,985 / 4.5yr vs +$205,025 flat-1ct, worst day -$1,610. VERIFY IN PAPER FIRST — two things TradersPost's docs do not settle: (1) whether 'Amount per position' divides by the option PREMIUM (correct) or the INDEX price (very wrong — SPX ~6,000 would size 0 contracts every day), and (2) whether an unaffordable day SKIPS or errors. The skip is where most of the edge lives, so confirm it on a real fill before trusting it.")
optContracts = input.int(3, "Option contracts (quantity)", minval=1, group="Bot1 · TradersPost", tooltip="Used only in 'Fixed contracts' mode. Default set to 3 on 2026-08-17 by user instruction (was briefly 10 in v1.2.2, which was not survivable — see WARNING 1). THIS IS THE ONLY SIZING FIELD THAT REACHES THE BROKER — initial_capital and default_qty_value affect the Strategy Tester display only, because the chart trades the INDEX, not the option. All backtest figures are PER CONTRACT: at 3ct the documented BOT1 worst day is -$20,940 against a $20,000 account (105%) WITHOUT the premium skip, and -$6,690 (33%) with it. Premium commits $2,400-$9,180 per entry, median $3,660. Median SPX premium ~$1,220/ct (p90 ~$5,400); risk/ct = half premium. The skip is what makes 3ct viable, and a flat contract count cannot apply it automatically — see the 'Bot1 - Risk' group below.")
optQtyFixed  = str.startswith(optQtyMode, "Fixed")

// --- Bot1 premium skip: RELATIVE to spot (replaces the drifting fixed-$ rule; see WARNING 3).
//     Pine cannot read option prices, so this only COMPUTES AND PRINTS the dollar threshold.
capOn  = input.bool(true, "Skip rich-premium days", group="Bot1 · Risk", tooltip="ON (default) prints a per-contract dollar ceiling on the entry label and in the BOT1 info alert. It does NOT and CANNOT block the order — a Pine chart has no access to option quotes. If the ATM ask is above the printed number, do not take the trade (or let TradersPost's 'Amount per position' do it for you). Turning this off only hides the number; it does not change any signal.")
capPct = input.float(0.70, "Skip if ATM premium > this % of spot", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group="Bot1 · Risk", tooltip="RELATIVE cap, so it does not drift as the index rises — the whole reason the old fixed $2,000 rule failed (0.49% of spot in 2022, 0.28% by 2026). 0.70 was chosen on the full 2022-2026 OPRA backtest: +$321,815 vs +$205,585 no-skip, PF 2.39, worst day -$2,230 vs -$6,980, max DD -$6,655 vs -$12,165, and it wins 4 of the 5 years. Walk-forward (each year's cap fit on prior years only) = +$183,490 vs +$147,080 across the 4 live years, so the gain is not pure hindsight. Threshold in DOLLARS per contract = spot x this % (SPX 7,800 x 0.70% = 54.6 points = $5,460). Lower it to trade less and cut the tail further; raise it toward 1.0 to trade almost everything.")
otmPct     = input.float(0.30, "Spread short leg OTM %", step=0.05, group="Bots 2/3 (retired)") * 0.01
strikeStep = input.float(5.0, "Strike spacing", group="Bots 2/3 (retired)")
enB2       = input.bool(false, "Bot2 30m spread alerts", group="Bots 2/3 (retired)", tooltip="OFF by default since v1.3.0 (2026-08-17): this is a ONE-BOT system now. Credit spreads were never webhook-automatable anyway (TradersPost sends single-leg orders only), so these were always manual. Tick to restore the chart labels and alertcondition()s.")
enB3       = input.bool(false, "Bot3 60m spread alerts", group="Bots 2/3 (retired)", tooltip="OFF by default since v1.3.0 (2026-08-17) — see the Bot2 tooltip. Note the 60m OR also has a single-leg long variant in pine/SPX_ORB_BOT3L_60M_v1_strategy.pine, which is likewise RETIRED under the one-bot decision; do not put it on a chart.")

isRTH  = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if barstate.isfirst and not (timeframe.isintraday and timeframe.multiplier == 5)
    runtime.error("SPX-ORB 3BOT requires a 5-minute chart.")
var int rthIx = na
rthIx := isRTH ? (na(rthIx[1]) or newDay ? 0 : nz(rthIx[1]) + 1) : na

// ==================== OR TRACKING ====================
var float hi15 = na, var float lo15 = na
var float hi30 = na, var float lo30 = na
var float hi60 = na, var float lo60 = na
if isRTH and rthIx == 0
    hi15 := high, lo15 := low
    hi30 := high, lo30 := low
    hi60 := high, lo60 := low
if isRTH and rthIx > 0
    if rthIx <= 2
        hi15 := math.max(hi15, high), lo15 := math.min(lo15, low)
    if rthIx <= 5
        hi30 := math.max(hi30, high), lo30 := math.min(lo30, low)
    if rthIx <= 11
        hi60 := math.max(hi60, high), lo60 := math.min(lo60, low)

// ==================== SIGNALS ====================
var int b1Dir = 0, var int b2Dir = 0, var int b3Dir = 0
var int b1Bar = na
if newDay
    b1Dir := 0, b2Dir := 0, b3Dir := 0, b1Bar := na
// v1.2.1: `rthIx < 77` blocks an entry on the FINAL bar of the session (15:55) — that entry can
// never be closed (the EOD failsafe skips the entry bar because position_size is still 0, there is
// no later RTH bar, and `newDay` nulls b1Bar so the time stop dies too), so it would carry to the
// next session while the 0DTE option expires. Same guard as SPX_ORB_BOT3L_60M_v1_strategy.pine.
b1Up = isRTH and rthIx > 2  and rthIx < 77 and b1Dir == 0 and close > hi15 * (1 + bufPct)
b1Dn = isRTH and rthIx > 2  and rthIx < 77 and b1Dir == 0 and close < lo15 * (1 - bufPct)
b2Up = enB2 and isRTH and rthIx > 5  and b2Dir == 0 and close > hi30 * (1 + bufPct)
b2Dn = enB2 and isRTH and rthIx > 5  and b2Dir == 0 and close < lo30 * (1 - bufPct)
b3Up = enB3 and isRTH and rthIx > 11 and b3Dir == 0 and close > hi60 * (1 + bufPct)
b3Dn = enB3 and isRTH and rthIx > 11 and b3Dir == 0 and close < lo60 * (1 - bufPct)

// ==================== BOT1 ORDERS (TradersPost options webhook) ====================
// TradingView alert message must be {{strategy.order.alert_message}} (same as the TSLA v3 setup).
// TradersPost: entries are always action=buy with optionType carrying direction (buy CALL up / buy PUT dn).
// Leave the opt-in "Invert puts" strategy setting UNCHECKED — with an explicit put contract in the signal,
// invert-ON would flip action=buy into SELL-TO-OPEN a short put.
// "+0 days" is safe to hardcode HERE because SPX lists an expiry EVERY trading day (true 0DTE daily);
// TSLA does NOT (~Mon/Wed/Fri only) — that's why the TSLA v3 strategy needs its expiration dropdown.
// v1.1: in "TradersPost sizing" mode the quantity field is OMITTED so TradersPost's own
// position sizing ("Amount per position") sets the contract count — an explicit quantity in
// the JSON would override it. Fixed mode is byte-identical to v1.0.
f_optMsg(action, cp) =>
    qpart = optQtyFixed ? '"quantity":' + str.tostring(optContracts) + ', ' : ''
    '{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"' + action + '", ' + qpart + '"expiration":"+0 days", "optionType":"' + cp + '", "strikesAway":0}'
// Per-contract dollar ceiling for the relative premium skip: spot points x cap% x $100/point,
// which reduces to spot x capPct. PRINTED ONLY — Pine has no option quotes (header WARNING 3).
b1SkipUsd = close * capPct
// display.data_window: off the price scale, but still selectable as a {{plot(...)}} alert
// placeholder (display.none removes it from that list too).
plot(b1SkipUsd, "B1 skip $", display=display.data_window)

if b1Up or b1Dn
    b1Dir := b1Up ? 1 : -1
    b1Bar := bar_index
    if b1Up
        strategy.entry("B1", strategy.long, alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "call"))
    else
        strategy.entry("B1", strategy.short, alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "put"))
    if capOn
        label.new(bar_index, b1Up ? low : high,
          "BOT1 BUY " + (b1Up ? "CALL" : "PUT") + " 0DTE ATM" + (optQtyFixed ? " x" + str.tostring(optContracts) : " (broker-sized)") +
          "\nSKIP IF ASK > $" + str.tostring(b1SkipUsd, "#,###") + " /ct  (" + str.tostring(capPct) + "% of spot)",
          style=b1Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
          color=color.new(color.teal, 15), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
tsBars = math.max(1, math.round(tsMin / 5.0))
b1TimeStop = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(b1Bar) and bar_index >= b1Bar + tsBars
b1EOD      = strategy.position_size != 0 and isRTH and rthIx >= 76      // 15:50 bar onward
if b1TimeStop or b1EOD
    // v1.1: no quantity on the exit — action=exit closes the WHOLE position. Required in
    // TradersPost-sizing mode (the strategy cannot know the broker-chosen contract count) and
    // safer in fixed mode too, where a stale quantity would leave a partial position open.
    strategy.close("B1", comment=b1TimeStop ? "Time stop " + str.tostring(tsMin) + "m" : "EOD",
         alert_message='{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"exit"}')

if b2Up or b2Dn
    b2Dir := b2Up ? 1 : -1
if b3Up or b3Dn
    b3Dir := b3Up ? 1 : -1

// ==================== SPREAD SUGGESTIONS + VISUALS ====================
psS = math.floor(close * (1 - otmPct) / strikeStep) * strikeStep
csS = math.ceil(close * (1 + otmPct) / strikeStep) * strikeStep
f0(x) => str.tostring(x, "#")
if b2Up or b2Dn
    label.new(bar_index, b2Up ? low : high,
      "BOT2 SELL 5-wide " + (b2Up ? "PUT spread " + f0(psS) + "/" + f0(psS - 5) : "CALL spread " + f0(csS) + "/" + f0(csS + 5)) + " 0DTE\nclose @50% credit · stop @2x",
      style=b2Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.blue, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
if b3Up or b3Dn
    label.new(bar_index, b3Up ? low : high,
      "BOT3 SELL 10-wide " + (b3Up ? "PUT spread " + f0(psS) + "/" + f0(psS - 10) : "CALL spread " + f0(csS) + "/" + f0(csS + 10)) + " 0DTE\nclose @50% credit · stop @2x",
      style=b3Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.purple, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 2  ? hi15 : na, "OR15 High", color.new(color.teal, 40),  2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 2  ? lo15 : na, "OR15 Low",  color.new(color.teal, 40),  2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 5  ? hi30 : na, "OR30 High", color.new(color.blue, 55),  1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 5  ? lo30 : na, "OR30 Low",  color.new(color.blue, 55),  1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? hi60 : na, "OR60 High", color.new(color.purple, 55),1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? lo60 : na, "OR60 Low",  color.new(color.purple, 55),1, plot.style_linebr)

// ==================== BOT1 INFO ALERT (premium ceiling) ====================
// The ORDER goes out through the strategy's alert_message (TradersPost JSON). This second,
// human-readable alert carries the skip threshold, which the JSON deliberately does NOT — an
// unknown key could be rejected by the broker bridge. Set it up as its own alert if you want the
// ceiling in your inbox; otherwise read it off the chart label.
alertcondition(b1Up and capOn, "BOT1 UP — buy CALL (with premium ceiling)",
     'SPX BOT1: 15m OR broke UP. BUY ATM 0DTE CALL. SKIP IF ASK > ${{plot("B1 skip $")}} per contract. Time stop 30m.')
alertcondition(b1Dn and capOn, "BOT1 DN — buy PUT (with premium ceiling)",
     'SPX BOT1: 15m OR broke DOWN. BUY ATM 0DTE PUT. SKIP IF ASK > ${{plot("B1 skip $")}} per contract. Time stop 30m.')

// ==================== SPREAD ALERTS (retired — enB2/enB3 default OFF since v1.3.0) ====================
alertcondition(b2Up, "BOT2 UP — sell PUT spread",  "SPX BOT2: 30m OR broke UP. SELL 5-wide PUT credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b2Dn, "BOT2 DN — sell CALL spread", "SPX BOT2: 30m OR broke DOWN. SELL 5-wide CALL credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b3Up, "BOT3 UP — sell PUT spread",  "SPX BOT3: 60m OR broke UP. SELL 10-wide PUT credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b3Dn, "BOT3 DN — sell CALL spread", "SPX BOT3: 60m OR broke DOWN. SELL 10-wide CALL credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
